  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "portal-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -130,
      "w": 520,
      "text": "The portal is a separate trust boundary, not the agent app with fields hidden.\nNo assignee, no internal notes, no SLA targets, no department. Story 09.",
      "page": "portal"
    },
    {
      "id": "rtl-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 560,
      "text": "Arabic flips everything, including the top chrome — that was the open question from the first draft.\nLatin stays LTR inside RTL text: ticket numbers, phone numbers, email, policy names.",
      "page": "arabic-foundations"
    },
    {
      "id": "spec-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 560,
      "text": "Ticket workspace is the primary spec — story 07 builds this screen.\nQueue left, conversation centre, context right. Everything else on this page reuses its vocabulary.",
      "page": "agent-app"
    },
    {
      "id": "search-option-a-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -140,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "Option A — reaches the language toggle. Fixes the edge-hugging bug (inset-inline-end:0) but the 540px panel spans two unrelated controls (search + language switcher), which can blur which one triggered it.",
      "page": "search-dropdown"
    },
    {
      "id": "search-option-b-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 560,
      "w": 460,
      "text": "Option B — anchored to the search field's own edge only, 480px, matching how the bell and user-menu dropdowns are each scoped to their own single trigger.",
      "page": "search-dropdown"
    },
    {
      "id": "search-option-c-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1260,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Option C — shipped. width: clamp(280px, 26vw, 480px) instead of a fixed anchor. Verified at 1024/1200/1440px: the panel is always a proportional fraction of the viewport, so it can never claim more room than the header actually has. This is what's live in GlobalSearch.tsx.",
      "page": "search-dropdown"
    },
    {
      "id": "search-problem-note",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 480,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "The problem with Option A, shown honestly: 1024px is GlobalSearch.tsx's own real breakpoint. The window below clips with overflow:hidden like a real viewport — Option A's fixed 540px panel runs past the edge and gets clipped, even placed more generously than its real position.",
      "page": "search-dropdown"
    },
    {
      "id": "search-mobile-note",
      "x": 1500,
      "y": 1980,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Mobile search is new UX, not an adaptation — there was no search entry point at all below the 1024px breakpoint. A full-screen takeover sidesteps the anchoring question entirely: no floating panel, no edge to hug.",
      "page": "search-dropdown"
    },
    {
      "id": "live-chat-note",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -160,
      "w": 640,
      "text": "Live chat used to be a Ticket shown in the ordinary queue and detail page — indistinguishable from email/WhatsApp. This redesign makes it a real messaging screen: a dedicated agent inbox (no SLA/category/priority/internal-note chrome) and a floating portal widget instead of a full-page navigation. The data model is unchanged — still channel=\"chat\" on the same Ticket — only the presentation is new.",
      "page": "live-chat"
    }
  ],
